<title>UK: Royal Bank appoints new group treasurer.</title>
<headline>Royal Bank appoints new group treasurer.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Bank of Scotland said on Thursday it has appointed Brian Crowe as group treasurer to replace Tim Good who has moved to the Halifax Building Society.</p>
<p>Crowe, 39, joins Royal Bank from Chase Manhattan Bank where he has been market risk executive for Europe and Asia.</p>
<p>Iain Robertson, Royal Bank managing director corporate and institutional banking, said the appointment would help the bank realise &quot;ambitions for further developments of our treasury and capital markets operations.&quot; -- London Newsroom +44 171 5642 7717.</p>
</text>
